---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import VoltCast from "../components/VoltCast.astro";
import "../styles/site.css";

const installUnix = "curl -fsSL https://volt-cli.dev/install.sh | sh";
const installWindows = "irm https://volt-cli.dev/install.ps1 | iex";
const title = "Volt — a coding agent from terminal to phone";
const description =
  "Volt is an open-source coding agent that runs on your computer. Start a conversation in the terminal and pick it up from your iPhone.";
const posts = (await getCollection("blog", ({ data }) => !data.draft)).sort(
  (left, right) => right.data.publishedAt.valueOf() - left.data.publishedAt.valueOf(),
);
const hasPublishedPosts = posts.length > 0;
const dateFormatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en", { dateStyle: "long", timeZone: "UTC" });
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f5f0" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://volt-cli.dev/" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/volt-icon.png" type="image/png" />
    <link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Volt Blog" href="/rss.xml" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-nav">
      <a class="brand" href="/">
        <img src="/volt-mark.svg" width="64" height="100" alt="" />
        volt
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        {hasPublishedPosts && <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>}
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="/docs/quickstart/">Quickstart</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/volt-hq/Volt">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="site-main">
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="kicker">Open source · Public beta</p>
        <h1>Your coding agent,<br />from terminal to phone.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Volt is a coding agent you use from your terminal. It runs on your own computer with the
          model subscription or API key you already have. When you step away, you can open the same
          conversation on your iPhone and keep going.
        </p>
        <div class="install" id="install-box" data-unix={installUnix} data-windows={installWindows}>
          <span class="install-legend" id="install-label">Install · macOS / Linux</span>
          <code id="install-cmd">{installUnix}</code>
          <button id="copy-btn" type="button" aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button>
          <span class="visually-hidden" id="copy-status" aria-live="polite"></span>
        </div>
        <p class="install-alt">
          or <code>npm install -g --ignore-scripts @hansjm10/volt-coding-agent</code>
          &nbsp;·&nbsp; <span id="install-other-label">Windows</span>:{" "}
          <code id="install-other-cmd">{installWindows}</code>
        </p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Get started</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/volt-hq/Volt">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="product-title">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="label">The terminal</p>
          <h2 id="product-title">What a session looks like</h2>
          <p>
            Here Volt is fixing a failing test in a small sample project. It reads the code, runs
            the tests, edits the function, and reruns the tests until they pass.
          </p>
          <p>
            Plan mode, subagents, session branching, and compaction are built in, and you can change
            the keybindings and theme. It works in tmux and over SSH, and it runs on Android through
            Termux.
          </p>
        </header>
        <figure class="product">
          <img
            class="shot"
            src="/docs-images/interactive-mode.png"
            width="1964"
            height="2536"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Volt terminal session in a sample project. Below the startup header, the user asks Volt to make a failing slugify test pass. Volt reads src/slugify.js, runs npm test and sees the failure, edits the file with an inline diff, reruns npm test successfully, and summarizes the fix. The editor and footer show the project path, git branch, session name, model, and context usage."
          />
          <figcaption class="margin-notes">
            <ol>
              <li>
                <p>
                  Tool calls show up inline as they run. Long output collapses so the transcript
                  stays readable, and <kbd>ctrl+o</kbd> expands it.
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  The label on the input box shows the mode. In Plan mode, Volt can only research,
                  and it asks you to approve a plan before it changes anything.
                </p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>
                  The footer has the working directory, branch, session name, model, how much context
                  you've used, and what the session has cost so far.
                </p>
              </li>
            </ol>
            <p class="shot-meta">Screenshot from Volt 0.2.1.</p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </section>

      <section class="section" id="phone" aria-labelledby="phone-title">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="label">Terminal to phone</p>
          <h2 id="phone-title">Continue from your iPhone</h2>
          <p>
            When you open a conversation in <code>volt</code>, it runs in a background daemon on your
            computer, not inside the terminal window. Your phone attaches to that same conversation,
            so you can close the terminal and keep going from the app. Iroh connects
            devices directly when possible and falls back to end-to-end encrypted relays.
          </p>
          <p>
            I built this because prompting a tmux session over SSH from my phone felt like using the
            wrong controller. I wrote about that in <a href="/blog/why-i-forked-pi-to-build-volt/">Why I Forked Pi to Build Volt</a>.
          </p>
        </header>

        <VoltCast />

        <figure class="pair">
          <img
            class="shot phone"
            src="/docs-images/shared-session-phone.png"
            width="603"
            height="1311"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Volt iOS app showing the conversation Discuss a Small Todo App in the volt workspace on branch fix/511-stale-default-models. The prompt Tell me about a small todo app, sent from the phone, is followed by the model's reply. The composer shows Build mode and the gpt-6-luna model."
          />
          <img
            class="shot"
            src="/docs-images/shared-session-terminal.png"
            width="1964"
            height="880"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="The same conversation open in the Volt terminal UI on the computer, showing the same prompt and reply. The footer shows the branch, session name, gpt-6-luna, and [phone 1], meaning one phone is attached."
          />
          <figcaption>
            The same conversation in the app and in the terminal. The prompt was sent from the phone,
            and <code>[phone 1]</code> in the terminal footer means a phone is attached. Screenshots
            from Volt 0.2.1.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="setup">
          <div>
            <h3>Pair a phone</h3>
            <pre class="commands"><code><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>volt daemon start
<span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>volt remote workspace add /path/to/project --name my-project
<span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">$ </span>volt remote pair --workspace my-project</code></pre>
            <p>
              You can also do all of this from <code>/remote</code> inside Volt. You only scan the QR
              code once. After that, the app remembers your computer.
            </p>
            <p class="links">
              <a href="/docs/quickstart/#continue-from-your-iphone">Set up phone access →</a>
              <a href="/docs/usage/#remote-access-over-iroh-preview">How remote access works →</a>
            </p>
          </div>
          <ul class="notes">
            <li>The iPhone app is in App Store review.</li>
            <li>
              Phone access needs the npm install (Node.js 22.19 or newer) on an Apple silicon Mac,
              Linux, or Windows. The standalone executables only work locally.
            </li>
            <li>Your computer has to stay on and reachable while you're away.</li>
            <li>
              The managed relay and completion notifications are part of Volt Pro. Direct and
              self-hosted connections are separate from Pro.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <details class="tour">
          <summary>Watch the 64-second tour</summary>
          <video
            controls
            playsinline
            preload="none"
            width="1920"
            height="1080"
            poster="/media/volt-showcase-poster.jpg"
            aria-label="Animated showcase: Volt plans and fixes a bug, and the conversation continues from an iPhone after the developer leaves the desk"
          >
            <source src="/media/volt-showcase.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <p>It has sound and captions.</p>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="more-title">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="label">More</p>
          <h2 id="more-title">What else Volt does</h2>
        </header>
        <dl class="specs">
          <div>
            <dt><a href="/docs/providers/">Models</a></dt>
            <dd>
              Sign in to a built-in provider with a subscription or an API key, or add any endpoint
              that speaks the OpenAI, Anthropic, or Google API. Anything else can be connected with an
              extension. You can switch models in the middle of a session.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt><a href="/docs/extensions/">Extensions</a></dt>
            <dd>
              The common coding-agent features are built in. Anything specific to your project goes
              in a skill, extension, prompt template, or Volt package. If the extension you need
              doesn't exist, you can ask Volt to write it.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt><a href="/docs/security/">Supply chain</a></dt>
            <dd>
              Direct dependencies are pinned to exact versions, the npm package ships with a
              shrinkwrap, and the installer runs npm with lifecycle scripts turned off. The docs also cover running Volt
              in a container if you want harder boundaries.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt><a href="/docs/sdk/">SDK and RPC</a></dt>
            <dd>
              The CLI runs on the same runtime you get through the SDK, RPC mode, and the JSON event
              stream, so you can build your own tools on top of it.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </section>

      {
        hasPublishedPosts && (
          <section class="section" aria-labelledby="writing-title">
            <header class="section-head split">
              <div>
                <p class="label">From the blog</p>
                <h2 id="writing-title">Recent posts</h2>
              </div>
              <a href="/blog/">All posts →</a>
            </header>
            <ol class="writing">
              {posts.slice(0, 2).map((post) => (
                <li>
                  <time datetime={post.data.publishedAt.toISOString()}>
                    {dateFormatter.format(post.data.publishedAt)}
                  </time>
                  <div>
                    <h3>
                      <a href={`/blog/${post.id}/`}>{post.data.title}</a>
                    </h3>
                    <p>{post.data.description}</p>
                  </div>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
          </section>
        )
      }
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <p>
        Maintained and distributed by{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/hansjm10">Jordan Hans</a>. Derived from{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/earendil-works/pi">Mario Zechner's Pi project</a>{" "}
        under the MIT License. Built in the open at{" "}
        <a href="https://github.com/volt-hq/Volt">github.com/volt-hq/Volt</a>.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Footer navigation">
        {hasPublishedPosts && <a href="/blog/">Blog</a>}
        <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
        <a href="/docs/security/">Security</a>
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/volt-hq/Volt/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contributing</a>
      </nav>
    </footer>

    <script>
      // Server-rendered default is macOS/Linux; swap to PowerShell on Windows hosts.
      const box = document.getElementById("install-box");
      const label = document.getElementById("install-label");
      const cmdEl = document.getElementById("install-cmd");
      const otherLabel = document.getElementById("install-other-label");
      const otherCmd = document.getElementById("install-other-cmd");
      const uaData = (navigator as Navigator & { userAgentData?: { platform?: string } }).userAgentData;
      const platform = uaData?.platform || navigator.platform || navigator.userAgent;
      if (/windows|win32|win64/i.test(platform) && box && label && cmdEl && otherLabel && otherCmd) {
        label.textContent = "Install · Windows";
        cmdEl.textContent = box.dataset.windows ?? "";
        otherLabel.textContent = "macOS / Linux";
        otherCmd.textContent = box.dataset.unix ?? "";
      }

      const btn = document.getElementById("copy-btn");
      const copyStatus = document.getElementById("copy-status");
      btn?.addEventListener("click", async () => {
        let message = "Copied the install command.";
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(cmdEl?.textContent ?? "");
          btn.textContent = "Copied";
        } catch {
          message = "Couldn't copy. Select the command and copy it.";
          btn.textContent = "Select and copy";
        }
        if (copyStatus) copyStatus.textContent = message;
        setTimeout(() => {
          btn.textContent = "Copy";
          if (copyStatus) copyStatus.textContent = "";
        }, 1500);
      });
    </script>

    <style>
      .hero {
        padding-block: 6rem 5.5rem;
      }

      .kicker {
        margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.1em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6.6vw, 4.75rem);
        font-weight: 700;
        line-height: 1.02;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
      }

      .lede {
        max-width: 38rem;
        margin: 1.6rem 0 2.6rem;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 1.15rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      /* Framed like the Volt TUI editor: a border with its legend set into the top edge. */
      .install {
        position: relative;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 1rem;
        max-width: 44rem;
        padding: 1.1rem 0.6rem 0.9rem 1.1rem;
        border: 1.5px solid var(--violet);
        border-radius: 4px;
      }

      .install-legend {
        position: absolute;
        top: 0;
        left: 0.8rem;
        padding-inline: 0.35rem;
        background: var(--paper);
        color: var(--violet);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.08em;
        line-height: 1;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        transform: translateY(-50%);
      }

      .install code {
        flex: 1;
        overflow-x: auto;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .install button {
        flex: none;
        padding: 0.3rem 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
        border-radius: 4px;
        background: transparent;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font: inherit;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      .install button:hover {
        border-color: var(--violet);
        color: var(--violet);
      }

      .install-alt {
        max-width: 44rem;
        margin: 0.9rem 0 0;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.82rem;
      }

      .install-alt code {
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      .cta {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.7rem;
        margin-top: 2.2rem;
      }

      .btn {
        display: inline-block;
        padding: 0.6rem 1.15rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
        border-radius: 5px;
        color: var(--ink);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .btn:hover {
        border-color: var(--ink);
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      .btn.primary {
        border-color: var(--ink);
        background: var(--ink);
        color: var(--paper);
      }

      .btn.primary:hover {
        border-color: var(--violet);
        background: var(--violet);
      }

      .section {
        padding-block: 5rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }

      .section-head {
        max-width: 42rem;
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
      }

      .section-head.split {
        display: flex;
        align-items: flex-end;
        justify-content: space-between;
        gap: 1rem 2rem;
        max-width: none;
      }

      .section h2 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.4vw, 2.3rem);
        line-height: 1.12;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      }

      .section-head p:not(.label) {
        margin: 1rem 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 1.05rem;
      }

      .section h3 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.35;
      }

      .section :not(pre) > code,
      .section kbd {
        padding: 0.1em 0.35em;
        border-radius: 3px;
        background: var(--paper-sunk);
        font-size: 0.88em;
      }

      .visually-hidden {
        position: absolute;
        width: 1px;
        height: 1px;
        overflow: hidden;
        clip-path: inset(50%);
        white-space: nowrap;
      }

      .shot {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        border-radius: 8px;
        background: var(--night);
      }

      .product {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 4fr);
        gap: 3rem;
        align-items: start;
        margin: 0;
      }

      .margin-notes {
        position: sticky;
        top: 2rem;
      }

      .margin-notes ol {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
        counter-reset: note;
      }

      .margin-notes li {
        padding-block: 1.1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
        counter-increment: note;
      }

      .margin-notes li:first-child {
        padding-top: 0;
        border-top: 0;
      }

      .margin-notes li::before {
        content: counter(note, decimal-leading-zero);
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
      }

      .margin-notes p {
        margin: 0;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .pair figcaption,
      .tour p {
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }

      .margin-notes .shot-meta {
        margin-top: 1.2rem;
        padding-top: 1.1rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
        color: var(--muted);
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }

      .pair {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 46fr) minmax(0, 223fr);
        gap: 1.25rem;
        align-items: start;
        margin: 4.5rem 0 0;
      }

      .shot.phone {
        border-radius: 18px;
      }

      .pair figcaption {
        grid-column: 1 / -1;
        max-width: 46rem;
      }

      .setup {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 4fr);
        gap: 3rem;
        margin-top: 3.5rem;
      }

      .setup h3 {
        margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
      }

      .commands {
        overflow-x: auto;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
        border-radius: 6px;
        background: var(--night);
        color: var(--night-text);
        font-size: 0.88rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .commands .prompt {
        color: #8d879a;
        user-select: none;
      }

      .setup p {
        margin: 1rem 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .setup .links {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.4rem 1.6rem;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .notes {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 0.9rem;
      }

      .notes li {
        padding-block: 0.7rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }

      .notes li:first-child {
        padding-top: 0;
        border-top: 0;
      }

      .tour {
        margin-top: 3rem;
      }

      .tour summary {
        width: fit-content;
        color: var(--violet);
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
      }

      .tour video {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 52rem;
        height: auto;
        aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
        margin-top: 1.2rem;
        border-radius: 8px;
        background: var(--night);
      }

      .tour p {
        margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
      }

      .specs {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 0 3rem;
        margin: 0;
      }

      .specs div {
        padding-block: 1.3rem 1.6rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }

      .specs dt {
        font-weight: 650;
      }

      .specs dt a {
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .specs dt a:hover {
        color: var(--violet);
      }

      .specs dd {
        margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
        font-size: 0.95rem;
      }

      .section-head.split > a {
        flex: none;
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      .writing {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
      }

      .writing li {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0, 1fr);
        gap: 0.4rem 2rem;
        padding-block: 1.5rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }

      .writing time {
        padding-top: 0.25rem;
        color: var(--muted);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: 0.8rem;
      }

      .writing h3 {
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      }

      .writing h3 a {
        color: var(--ink);
      }

      .writing h3 a:hover {
        color: var(--violet);
      }

      .writing p {
        max-width: 40rem;
        margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }

      @media (max-width: 860px) {
        .product,
        .setup {
          grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        }

        .margin-notes {
          position: static;
        }

        .pair {
          grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        }

        .shot.phone {
          width: min(60%, 16rem);
        }

        .pair .shot:not(.phone) {
          grid-row: 1;
        }
      }

      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .hero {
          padding-block: 3.5rem 3.5rem;
        }

        .install {
          flex-direction: column;
          align-items: stretch;
          gap: 0.7rem;
          padding-right: 1.1rem;
        }

        .install code {
          white-space: pre-wrap;
          overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }

        .install button {
          align-self: flex-start;
        }

        .section {
          padding-block: 3.5rem;
        }

        .specs {
          grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        }

        .writing li {
          grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
        }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
